  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-108074",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite $256$ as a power of $2$ (the base of the logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n256={2}^{8}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n{log}_{2}⁡256={log}_{2}⁡({2}^{8})\n$$\n\nThe logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n{log}_{b}⁡({b}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $b=2$ and $x=8.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n{log}_{2}⁡({2}^{8})=8\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
